  "progression": {
    "years-one-two": "Programming precedes data structures, programming languages and operating systems. Discrete mathematics, linear algebra and programming support the advanced algorithms, numerical and visual computing courses. The prior programming and project courses are recommended for the year-two software engineering project.",
    "third-year": "30 EC of open elective space, 12 EC selected from three restricted courses, then the 18 EC project. The selected Compiler Construction follows the recommended knowledge from years one and two. Classical Cryptography recommends pre-university mathematics.",
    "final-project": "Finish both first years in full. Timely applicants with 144 EC or more have direct entry. The coordinator considers applicants at 126 EC or more but below 144 EC, and entry is unavailable below 126 EC. The ordinary sequence reaches 162 EC before the project."
